We need to produce SHACL shapes that represent the requirement TRF-050 clause 4.4.4.2: frames attached to shell by double continuous weld; no scalloping allowed except when crossing shell plate butts.

Given ontology terms: frameAttachmentRecord class, object properties: frameAttachment (from frame to frameAttachmentRecord), frameShellWeldType (domain frameAttachmentRecord, range weldTypeValue). Data properties: scallopingPresent (domain frameAttachmentRecord boolean), shellPlateButtCrossing (domain frameAttachmentRecord boolean). Also an individual doubleContinuousWeld of type weldTypeValue.

Goal: create SHACL shape targeting frameAttachmentRecord (as per contract target_owner). Must enforce that frameShellWeldType = doubleContinuousWeld, scallopingPresent false, and shellPlateButtCrossing boolean may be true only if scallopingPresent false? Actually rule: No scalloping allowed except when crossing shell plate butts. That means if shellPlateButtCrossing true, scallopingPresent may be true? Wait phrase: "No scalloping is allowed (except when crossing shell plate butts)." So scalloping is allowed only when crossing shell plate butts. Therefore constraint: scallopingPresent must be false unless shellPlateButtCrossing is true – i.e., scallopingPresent implies shellPlateButtCrossing. Equivalent: if scallopingPresent true then shellPlateButtCrossing true. Could also enforce that when shellPlateButtCrossing true, scallopingPresent can be true or false? The phrase: allowed exception: scalloping is allowed when crossing shell plate butts. So scalloping present only permissible when crossing butts. So shape: if scallopingPresent = true then shellPlateButtCrossing must be true. Could also enforce that scallopingPresent = false when shellPlateButtCrossing false, but we might not need to enforce.

Also weld type must be doubleContinuousWeld; likely must be exactly that individual.

We must use property paths: the property for weld type is frameShellWeldType, which is object property linking to weldTypeValue individuals. So shape will contain sh:property with sh:path vocab:frameShellWeldType, sh:hasValue <doubleContinuousWeld>.

Similarly for scallopingPresent, use sh:property with sh:path vocab:scallopingPresent, sh:datatype xsd:boolean, sh:maxCount 1, sh:minCount 1? Possibly optional, but spec may require presence. Not given whether mandatory, but we can require value present.

May need sh:or for conditional rule: if scallopingPresent true then shellPlateButtCrossing true. In SHACL, we can use sh:if ... sh:then pattern using sh:property shapes? Actually SHACL allows sh:if/sh:then/sh:else constructs at node shape level. Use sh:if with an inner shape that tests scallopingPresent true, then sh:then with shape requiring shellPlateButtCrossing true. Example: sh:if [sh:property [sh:path vocab:scallopingPresent; sh:hasValue true]]; sh:then [sh:property [sh:path vocab:shellPlateButtCrossing; sh:hasValue true]].

Alternatively use sh:property with sh:or: either scallopingPresent false, or both true.

